  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements**\n\nI\'m diving into the user\'s prompt. It outlines the DevSecOps squad\'s mission: building \"App 3: ReconCorrelator - Orquestrador de Superf\303\255cie de.\" I\'m dissecting this title and the squad structure to understand the core requirements and establish a baseline for analysis. The prompt has provided a good start for this phase.\n\n\n**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to defining the **ReconCorrelator**\'s complete implementation, given the new urgency regarding the application not appearing. The requirements are now clearly defined into three key modules: Red Team Command Interface, Scope & Target Management with OPSEC & Scope Guard, and the Multi-Tool Parsers & Ingestion Engine, with a focus on delivering a world-class implementation.\n\n\n**Developing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now deep in thought about the **ReconCorrelator\'s** architecture. I\'m focusing on key modules. I\'m visualizing built-in sample datasets for immediate testing and visualization. The *Recon Correlation Brain* will auto-correlate domains, IPs, ports, and vulnerabilities, and flag high-priority attack vectors. I\'m also planning the *Interactive Attack Surface Visualizer* - a dynamic, interactive graph.\n\n\n**Constructing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the user interface for this application. I\'ve been giving lots of thought to the *Live Assets Triage Matrix*, with an aim to make it an incredibly dense, high-utility hacker interface. I\'m focusing on quick filters, sorting, search functionality, and export options, as well as actionable exploration links. I\'m also planning the *Orchestrator Pipeline* and a CLI execution simulator for custom recon pipelines.\n\n\n**Designing the Components**\n\nI\'m now deep in code design. I\'m focusing on incorporating real-time test execution directly into the UI, complete with assertion visualizations and status logs. The core data structures are taking shape, and I\'m designing parsers for various recon tools like subfinder, amass, and httpx, with parsers for nmap and nuclei also planned. Furthermore, I\'m thinking how to integrate AI threat intelligence to augment attack vector analysis.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Elements**\n\nI\'m now outlining key components and data structures. I\'m focusing on the Nuclei JSON output parser, scope validation with CIDR and wildcard logic, the master correlation engine, and ready-to-use sample data. I\'m also planning automated tests for parsers, scope guards, correlation logic, and resilience. I am focusing on developing components such as a header with badges and quick stats, an interactive attack surface graph, a triaged assets table, and a recon pipeline runner.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 345692872
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
