    thinking: "**Refining Header Inputs**\n\nI\'m updating the default header suggestions, considering both \"HackerOne-Research\" and \"BugBounty-Hacker\" formats. I\'m also exploring custom header inputs and ways to manage default project settings. I need to make sure the user has flexibility in header creation.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Graphs**\n\nI\'m working on an interactive attack graph. I\'m focusing on user control, specifically adding zoom features with the mouse wheel and buttons, along with panning by dragging the background. I am implementing click-and-drag functionality for nodes, with real-time edge updates, and a reset button. A full, interactive Linux terminal is also being worked on, so I can use hacker tools directly.\n\n\n**Integrating Terminal Commands**\n\nI\'m focused on integrating a powerful Linux terminal. I\'m building a bash-like shell with autocomplete, history, and color support. I\'m prioritizing direct command execution against the API. Initial commands will include subdomain enumeration tools like subfinder and dnsx, along with HTTP probing utilities like httpx and curl, using my preferred header.\n\n\n"
