  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Identification Headers**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the identification headers needed for the HackerOne platform, specifically `X-HackerOne-Research` with the value `w0rmingstar`. I\'m also considering the `X-BugBounty-Hunter` header.\n\n\n**Implementing User-Agent Standardization**\n\nI\'m now implementing the standardized user agent within all tools. My focus is on ensuring `User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (SecurityResearch; BugBounty; w0rmingstar@hackerone)` is honored across cURL generators, playbooks, and terminal commands. I\'m also adding flexible customization through the UI or terminal, allowing dynamic header changes.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Graph**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive graph design within the application. I\'m implementing drag-and-drop node functionality with real-time edge updates. Node positions are tracked in the state, utilizing `customPositions`. I\'m also adding layout presets like \"Radial\" and \"Force Directed.\" User hover will instantly show stats. Also the addition of an export graph as PNG / SVG button will make my toolkit complete.\n\n\n**Creating Command-Line Interface**\n\nI\'m currently designing the command-line interface. I\'m focusing on commands like `help`, `target`, and `header` for easy navigation. I\'m also adding specialized modules like `crtsh`, `subfinder`, `dnsx`, `httpx`, and `curl`, each with unique functionalities for subdomain enumeration, DNS resolution, and HTTP probing. Each command will be tailored with specific flags for enhanced customization. All this will be directly linked to the application\'s graph state.\n\n\n**Developing Command Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing new command-line functionalities. The focus is on incorporating commands like `wayback` for extracting archived URLs, `nuclei` for fast vulnerability triage, and `nmap` for service banner grabbing and port mapping. I\'m also adding multi-stage pipelines with `scan --all` / `recon-all` and a feature to scan for orphan CNAME takeovers using the `takeovers` command. I\'m also building out useful features to `assets`, `vulns`, and exporting the attack surface using the `export` command. Lastly, `gemini` / `ai` will offer AI Co-Pilot command for threat analysis.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 304138942
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
