  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Default Headers**\n\nI\'m focusing on default header behavior in `ReconPlaybookGenerator`. My current thought is about how to handle cases where a `target.policy?.requiredHeaders?.[0]` isn\'t specified. I\'m thinking we should default the header to `X-HackerOne-Research: w0rmingstar` (or whatever the user designates). This needs `headerFlag` to default to `-H \"X-HackerOne-Research: w0rmingstar\"`.\n\n\n**Designing Attack Graph Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the requirements for `components/AttackGraph.tsx`. I\'m focused on implementing interactive pan and zoom capabilities within the SVG container. Also, I\'m thinking about how to handle dragging individual nodes, using a `nodePositions` state to track user-defined node positions. I\'m exploring an approach to prevent canvas drag when dragging a node.\n\n\n**Implementing Graph Features**\n\nMy mind is now on graph enhancements. I\'m prioritizing features like node search with highlighting, alongside auto-scroll and center functionalities. I\'m also considering filter toggles for IPs, ports, vulnerabilities, and alive nodes. Additionally, I\'m thinking about a fullscreen mode toggle. I\'m exploring a selection drawer with asset details and quick PoC snippets. Lastly, I\'m focusing on exporting options, with SVG and JSON formats.\n\n**Designing a Terminal Arsenal**\n\nI\'m now shifting focus to the terminal implementation. I need a usable Linux terminal with a full arsenal of tools. I want the tool to be simple to use, but extremely powerful.\n\n\n**Defining Terminal Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the commands and quick bar features for the Arsenal Terminal. I\'m imagining a Linux-style prompt with styling, history, and autocomplete. I\'m designing a quick bar for rapid command execution, including tools for full recon, subfinder, httpx, takeover audits, wayback, nuclei, AI triage, and H1 reports. I\'m also planning executable commands like `target` and `header`.\n\n\n**Defining Terminal Commands**\n\nI\'m now focusing on terminal functionality. I\'ve designed commands for subdomain enumeration and web probing, including `subfinder`, `crtsh`, `dnsx`, `dig`, `httpx`, `wayback`, `katana`, `nuclei`, and `takeovers`, all accessible via API. Furthermore, I\'ve integrated asset and vulnerability listings, and a few common utilities like `curl`. Finally, I\'ve got exporting capabilities in mind.\n\n\n**Defining Terminal Commands**\n\nI\'ve been working on specific commands and functionality. I\'m implementing commands like `md` for report generation, `gemini` or `ai` to use Gemini for analysis, `clear`, `history`, `whois`, `scope`, and `recon-flow` to visualize recon phases. I\'m focusing on the communication of the terminal with the global state, using the hooks passed from `app/page.tsx` for data and control. Now, I\'m checking the `lib/sampleData.ts` file.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 234904525
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
