    thinking: "**Defining Terminal Capabilities**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the `TerminalArsenal.tsx` component, envisioning a terminal loaded with recon and pentest utilities. I\'m prioritizing functionalities needed to empower the user with a powerful terminal experience. My goal is to determine the ideal feature set, ensuring it delivers a comprehensive environment for hacking.\n\n\n**Enhancing Terminal Interface**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the visual and user experience elements. I\'m aiming for a familiar Linux-style bash prompt to establish that terminal feel. I\'m implementing color-coded ANSI output for clarity, and command history navigation for ease of use. Auto-completion is my focus now, covering commands and relevant domains, and I\'m developing a Quick Arsenal Dock for streamlined operations. My goal is to maximize functionality for a superior hacking experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Command Suite**\n\nI\'ve been adding many new commands to the arsenal. I\'ve integrated `wayback`, `nuclei`, and `gemini` for data retrieval, vulnerability scanning, and exploit assistance, respectively. I also added `curl -I`, and `takeovers` for specific audits, alongside `assets` and `vulns` for presenting the results. Reporting has been streamlined with `h1-report`. The `scope`, `header`, and `target` commands are also now integrated, along with basics such as `clear`, `help`, and `man`. I am now focusing on terminal user experience elements.\n\n\n"
