  planner_response {
    response: "# [RELAT\303\223RIO DE ENGENHARIA - FASE 1: PERSIST\303\212NCIA DE DADOS]\n\n**Aos cuidados do L\303\255der de Opera\303\247\303\265es:** O Squad (Delta & Beta) concluiu o planejamento e a modelagem da **Fase 1 (Banco de Dados Local SQLite Ass\303\255ncrono com SQLAlchemy / aiosqlite)**.\n\nSeguindo o protocolo estrito de TDD (Test-Driven Development), apresentamos primeiramente a suite de testes unit\303\241rios desenvolvida por **Delta (QA)** e, em seguida, a arquitetura e implementa\303\247\303\243o proposta por **Beta (Backend)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. \360\237\233\241\357\270\217 DELTA (QA) \342\200\224 Casos de Teste (PyTest + Asyncio)\n\nOs testes utilizam banco de dados SQLite isolado em mem\303\263ria (`sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:`) para garantir execu\303\247\303\243o instant\303\242nea e sem efeitos colaterais no ambiente do Arch Linux.\n\n### `tests/test_persistence.py`\n\n```python\nimport pytest\nimport pytest_asyncio\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n\nfrom src.database.models import Base, Program, Scope, ScopeType, Asset\nfrom src.database.repository import ReconRepository\nfrom src.database.exceptions import OutOfScopeAssetException\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def async_session():\n    \"\"\"Cria um banco SQLite em mem\303\263ria isolado para cada teste.\"\"\"\n    engine = create_async_engine(\"sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:\", echo=False)\n    async with engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    async_session_factory = sessionmaker(\n        engine, expire_on_commit=False, class_=AsyncSession\n    )\n    \n    async with async_session_factory() as session:\n        yield session\n\n    await engine.dispose()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_create_program_and_scopes(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 1: Testa a inser\303\247\303\243o de um novo Program e seus Scopes (In-Scope e Out-of-Scope).\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    # 1. Cria o Programa\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"Uber Bug Bounty\")\n    assert program.id is not None\n    assert program.name == \"Uber Bug Bounty\"\n    assert program.created_at is not None\n\n    # 2. Insere escopos\n    scope_in = await repo.add_scope(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        domain=\"*.uber.com\",\n        scope_type=ScopeType.IN_SCOPE\n    )\n    scope_out = await repo.add_scope(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        domain=\"internal-admin.uber.com\",\n        scope_type=ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE\n    )\n\n    assert scope_in.id is not None\n    assert scope_in.scope_type == ScopeType.IN_SCOPE\n    assert scope_out.domain == \"internal-admin.uber.com\"\n    assert scope_out.scope_type == ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_persistence_reload(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 2: Garante que os dados persistem e podem ser recarregados\n    com todos os relacionamentos intactos.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"HackerOne Acme\")\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.acme.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n    \n    # Recarrega do banco\n    loaded_program = await repo.get_program_by_id(program.id)\n    assert loaded_program is not None\n    assert len(loaded_program.scopes) == 1\n    assert loaded_program.scopes[0].domain == \"*.acme.com\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_insert_asset_in_scope_success(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 3: Insere ativo v\303\241lido dentro do escopo com sucesso.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"HackerOne Acme\")\n    scope = await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.acme.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n\n    asset = await repo.add_asset(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        subdomain=\"api.acme.com\",\n        resolved_ip=\"104.16.12.34\"\n    )\n\n    assert asset.id is not None\n    assert asset.subdomain == \"api.acme.com\"\n    assert asset.resolved_ip == \"104.16.12.34\"\n    assert asset.scope_id == scope.id\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_reject_asset_out_of_scope(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 4 (Restri\303\247\303\243o Cr\303\255tica): N\303\243o permite cadastrar subdom\303\255nios \n    que perten\303\247am a um dom\303\255nio explicitamente marcado como \'Out-of-Scope\'.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"Uber Bug Bounty\")\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.uber.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"internal-admin.uber.com\", ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE)\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.corp.uber.com\", ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE)\n\n    # 1. Tentativa de inserir ativo exato out-of-scope -> DEVE FALHAR\n    with pytest.raises(OutOfScopeAssetException) as exc_info:\n        await repo.add_asset(\n            program_id=program.id,\n            subdomain=\"internal-admin.uber.com\",\n            resolved_ip=\"10.0.0.1\"\n        )\n    assert \"Out-of-Scope\" in str(exc_info.value)\n\n    # 2. Tentativa de inserir ativo wildcard out-of-scope -> DEVE FALHAR\n    with pytest.raises(OutOfScopeAssetException):\n        await repo.add_asset(\n            program_id=program.id,\n            subdomain=\"vault.corp.uber.com\",\n            resolved_ip=\"10.0.0.2\"\n        )\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. \342\232\231\357\270\217 BETA (BACKEND) \342\200\224 Arquitetura & Implementa\303\247\303\243o SQLite / SQLAlchemy\n\nEstrutura implementada para garantir chamadas ass\303\255ncronas sem travar a interface e valida\303\247\303\243o de escopos em conformidade com as regras de Safe Harbor.\n\n### 2.1. Modelos de Dados (`src/database/models.py`)\n\n```python\nimport enum\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom sqlalchemy import (\n    Column,\n    Integer,\n    String,\n    DateTime,\n    ForeignKey,\n    Enum as SqlEnum,\n    UniqueConstraint\n)\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, relationship\n\nBase = declarative_base()\n\n\nclass ScopeType(str, enum.Enum):\n    IN_SCOPE = \"in_scope\"\n    OUT_OF_SCOPE = \"out_of_scope\"\n\n\nclass Program(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"programs\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    name = Column(String(255), nullable=False, unique=True)\n    created_at = Column(\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\n        default=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        nullable=False\n    )\n\n    # Relacionamentos\n    scopes = relationship(\"Scope\", back_populates=\"program\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\", lazy=\"selectin\")\n    assets = relationship(\"Asset\", back_populates=\"program\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\", lazy=\"selectin\")\n\n\nclass Scope(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"scopes\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    program_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"programs.id\", ondelete=\"CASCADE\"), nullable=False)\n    domain = Column(String(255), nullable=False)\n    scope_type = Column(SqlEnum(ScopeType), nullable=False, default=ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n\n    program = relationship(\"Program\", back_populates=\"scopes\")\n    assets = relationship(\"Asset\", back_populates=\"scope\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\")\n\n    __table_args__ = (\n        UniqueConstraint(\"program_id\", \"domain\", \"scope_type\", name=\"uq_program_domain_scope\"),\n    )\n\n\nclass Asset(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"assets\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    program_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"programs.id\", ondelete=\"CASCADE\"), nullable=False)\n    scope_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"scopes.id\", ondelete=\"SET NULL\"), nullable=True)\n    subdomain = Column(String(255), nullable=False)\n    resolved_ip = Column(String(64), nullable=True)\n    discovered_at = Column(\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\n        default=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        nullable=False\n    )\n\n    program = relationship(\"Program\", back_populates=\"assets\")\n    scope = relationship(\"Scope\", back_populates=\"assets\")\n\n    __table_args__ = (\n        UniqueConstraint(\"program_id\", \"subdomain\", name=\"uq_program_subdomain\"),\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.2. Validador de Escopo (`src/database/scope_validator.py`)\n\n```python\nimport fnmatch\nfrom typing import List\nfrom src.database.models import Scope, ScopeType\nfrom src.database.exceptions import OutOfScopeAssetException, NoMatchingInScopeException\n\n\nclass ScopeValidator:\n    \"\"\"Valida se um subdom\303\255nio descoberto \303\251 eleg\303\255vel com base nas regras do programa.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def domain_matches_pattern(subdomain: str, pattern: str) -> bool:\n        subdomain = subdomain.lower().strip()\n        pattern = pattern.lower().strip()\n\n        if pattern.startswith(\"*.\"):\n            base_domain = pattern[2:]\n            # Ex: *.uber.com d\303\241 match em api.uber.com e uber.com\n            return subdomain == base_domain or subdomain.endswith(\".\" + base_domain)\n        \n        return fnmatch.fnmatch(subdomain, pattern)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def validate_and_match_scope(cls, subdomain: str, scopes: List[Scope]) -> Scope:\n        # 1. Primeiro verifica se viola alguma regra de OUT-OF-SCOPE\n        for scope in scopes:\n            if scope.scope_type == ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE:\n                if cls.domain_matches_pattern(subdomain, scope.domain):\n                    raise OutOfScopeAssetException(\n                        f\"Ativo \'{subdomain}\' pertence \303\240 regra Out-of-Scope: \'{scope.domain}\'\"\n                    )\n\n        # 2. Verifica se encaixa em alguma regra IN-SCOPE\n        matched_in_scope = None\n        for scope in scopes:\n            if scope.scope_type == ScopeType.IN_SCOPE:\n                if cls.domain_matches_pattern(subdomain, scope.domain):\n                    matched_in_scope = scope\n                    break\n\n        if not matched_in_scope:\n            raise NoMatchingInScopeException(\n                f\"Ativo \'{subdomain}\' n\303\243o pertence a nenhum escopo In-Scope cadastrado.\"\n            )\n\n        return matched_in_scope\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.3. Reposit\303\263rio Ass\303\255ncrono com Auto-Migra\303\247\303\243o (`src/database/repository.py`)\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.future import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n\nfrom src.database.models import Base, Program, Scope, ScopeType, Asset\nfrom src.database.scope_validator import ScopeValidator\n\n\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    \"\"\"Gerencia conex\303\243o SQLite e migra\303\247\303\265es autom\303\241ticas de inicializa\303\247\303\243o.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = \"recon.db\"):\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.engine = create_async_engine(f\"sqlite+aiosqlite:///{db_path}\", echo=False)\n        self.session_factory = sessionmaker(\n            self.engine, expire_on_commit=False, class_=AsyncSession\n        )\n\n    async def init_db(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifica se o banco existe e cria as tabelas automaticamente.\"\"\"\n        async with self.engine.begin() as conn:\n            await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    def get_session(self) -> AsyncSession:\n        return self.session_factory()\n\n\nclass ReconRepository:\n    def __init__(self, session: AsyncSession):\n        self.session = session\n\n    async def create_program(self, name: str) -> Program:\n        program = Program(name=name)\n        self.session.add(program)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(program)\n        return program\n\n    async def get_program_by_id(self, program_id: int) -> Optional[Program]:\n        result = await self.session.execute(\n            select(Program).where(Program.id == program_id)\n        )\n        return result.scalars().first()\n\n    async def add_scope(self, program_id: int, domain: str, scope_type: ScopeType) -> Scope:\n        scope = Scope(program_id=program_id, domain=domain, scope_type=scope_type)\n        self.session.add(scope)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(scope)\n        return scope\n\n    async def add_asset(self, program_id: int, subdomain: str, resolved_ip: Optional[str] = None) -> Asset:\n        program = await self.get_program_by_id(program_id)\n        if not program:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Programa ID {program_id} n\303\243o encontrado.\")\n\n        # Valida\303\247\303\243o contra In-Scope e Out-of-Scope antes da inser\303\247\303\243o\n        matched_scope = ScopeValidator.validate_and_match_scope(subdomain, program.scopes)\n\n        asset = Asset(\n            program_id=program_id,\n            scope_id=matched_scope.id,\n            subdomain=subdomain,\n            resolved_ip=resolved_ip\n        )\n        self.session.add(asset)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(asset)\n        return asset\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. \360\237\216\257 Valida\303\247\303\243o da Fase 1\n\nTodos os 4 cen\303\241rios de teste exigidos por Delta foram cobertos:\n1. Inser\303\247\303\243o de `Program` e `Scope` (In/Out-of-Scope).\n2. Persist\303\252ncia e recarregamento relacional ass\303\255ncrono.\n3. Inser\303\247\303\243o bem-sucedida de subdom\303\255nios in-scope.\n4. **Bloqueio r\303\255gido de subdom\303\255nios pertencentes ao Out-of-Scope** (via exact match e wildcard matching).\n\n---\n\n> **L\303\255der de Opera\303\247\303\265es:** Voc\303\252 est\303\241 satisfeito com a arquitetura de persist\303\252ncia e a su\303\255te de testes da **FASE 1**, ou deseja algum ajuste no schema/regras antes de avan\303\247armos para a **FASE 2 (Motor de Execu\303\247\303\243o de Subprocessos / Terminal Resiliente)**?"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mission Directive**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s \"NOVA DIRETRIZ DE MISS\303\203O.\" The focus is on a resilience and UX upgrade, specifically version 1.1. Phase one seems to be data persistence, using a local SQLite database. I\'m noting the strategic implications.\n\n\n**Structuring Phase Execution**\n\nNow I\'m structuring the response to strictly follow the FASE 1 persistence steps. My current focus is on presenting the PyTest cases for the database and data models (Targets/Scopes) as Delta, and then the SQLite architecture and code using SQLAlchemy/Aiosqlite as Beta. I plan to rigorously adhere to this protocol, waiting for approval before moving to the next phase.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# [RELAT\303\223RIO DE ENGENHARIA - FASE 1: PERSIST\303\212NCIA DE DADOS]\n\n**Aos cuidados do L\303\255der de Opera\303\247\303\265es:** O Squad (Delta & Beta) concluiu o planejamento e a modelagem da **Fase 1 (Banco de Dados Local SQLite Ass\303\255ncrono com SQLAlchemy / aiosqlite)**.\n\nSeguindo o protocolo estrito de TDD (Test-Driven Development), apresentamos primeiramente a suite de testes unit\303\241rios desenvolvida por **Delta (QA)** e, em seguida, a arquitetura e implementa\303\247\303\243o proposta por **Beta (Backend)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. \360\237\233\241\357\270\217 DELTA (QA) \342\200\224 Casos de Teste (PyTest + Asyncio)\n\nOs testes utilizam banco de dados SQLite isolado em mem\303\263ria (`sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:`) para garantir execu\303\247\303\243o instant\303\242nea e sem efeitos colaterais no ambiente do Arch Linux.\n\n### `tests/test_persistence.py`\n\n```python\nimport pytest\nimport pytest_asyncio\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n\nfrom src.database.models import Base, Program, Scope, ScopeType, Asset\nfrom src.database.repository import ReconRepository\nfrom src.database.exceptions import OutOfScopeAssetException\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def async_session():\n    \"\"\"Cria um banco SQLite em mem\303\263ria isolado para cada teste.\"\"\"\n    engine = create_async_engine(\"sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:\", echo=False)\n    async with engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    async_session_factory = sessionmaker(\n        engine, expire_on_commit=False, class_=AsyncSession\n    )\n    \n    async with async_session_factory() as session:\n        yield session\n\n    await engine.dispose()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_create_program_and_scopes(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 1: Testa a inser\303\247\303\243o de um novo Program e seus Scopes (In-Scope e Out-of-Scope).\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    # 1. Cria o Programa\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"Uber Bug Bounty\")\n    assert program.id is not None\n    assert program.name == \"Uber Bug Bounty\"\n    assert program.created_at is not None\n\n    # 2. Insere escopos\n    scope_in = await repo.add_scope(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        domain=\"*.uber.com\",\n        scope_type=ScopeType.IN_SCOPE\n    )\n    scope_out = await repo.add_scope(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        domain=\"internal-admin.uber.com\",\n        scope_type=ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE\n    )\n\n    assert scope_in.id is not None\n    assert scope_in.scope_type == ScopeType.IN_SCOPE\n    assert scope_out.domain == \"internal-admin.uber.com\"\n    assert scope_out.scope_type == ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_persistence_reload(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 2: Garante que os dados persistem e podem ser recarregados\n    com todos os relacionamentos intactos.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"HackerOne Acme\")\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.acme.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n    \n    # Recarrega do banco\n    loaded_program = await repo.get_program_by_id(program.id)\n    assert loaded_program is not None\n    assert len(loaded_program.scopes) == 1\n    assert loaded_program.scopes[0].domain == \"*.acme.com\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_insert_asset_in_scope_success(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 3: Insere ativo v\303\241lido dentro do escopo com sucesso.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"HackerOne Acme\")\n    scope = await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.acme.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n\n    asset = await repo.add_asset(\n        program_id=program.id,\n        subdomain=\"api.acme.com\",\n        resolved_ip=\"104.16.12.34\"\n    )\n\n    assert asset.id is not None\n    assert asset.subdomain == \"api.acme.com\"\n    assert asset.resolved_ip == \"104.16.12.34\"\n    assert asset.scope_id == scope.id\n\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_reject_asset_out_of_scope(async_session: AsyncSession):\n    \"\"\"\n    Delta Test 4 (Restri\303\247\303\243o Cr\303\255tica): N\303\243o permite cadastrar subdom\303\255nios \n    que perten\303\247am a um dom\303\255nio explicitamente marcado como \'Out-of-Scope\'.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo = ReconRepository(async_session)\n\n    program = await repo.create_program(name=\"Uber Bug Bounty\")\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.uber.com\", ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"internal-admin.uber.com\", ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE)\n    await repo.add_scope(program.id, \"*.corp.uber.com\", ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE)\n\n    # 1. Tentativa de inserir ativo exato out-of-scope -> DEVE FALHAR\n    with pytest.raises(OutOfScopeAssetException) as exc_info:\n        await repo.add_asset(\n            program_id=program.id,\n            subdomain=\"internal-admin.uber.com\",\n            resolved_ip=\"10.0.0.1\"\n        )\n    assert \"Out-of-Scope\" in str(exc_info.value)\n\n    # 2. Tentativa de inserir ativo wildcard out-of-scope -> DEVE FALHAR\n    with pytest.raises(OutOfScopeAssetException):\n        await repo.add_asset(\n            program_id=program.id,\n            subdomain=\"vault.corp.uber.com\",\n            resolved_ip=\"10.0.0.2\"\n        )\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. \342\232\231\357\270\217 BETA (BACKEND) \342\200\224 Arquitetura & Implementa\303\247\303\243o SQLite / SQLAlchemy\n\nEstrutura implementada para garantir chamadas ass\303\255ncronas sem travar a interface e valida\303\247\303\243o de escopos em conformidade com as regras de Safe Harbor.\n\n### 2.1. Modelos de Dados (`src/database/models.py`)\n\n```python\nimport enum\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom sqlalchemy import (\n    Column,\n    Integer,\n    String,\n    DateTime,\n    ForeignKey,\n    Enum as SqlEnum,\n    UniqueConstraint\n)\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, relationship\n\nBase = declarative_base()\n\n\nclass ScopeType(str, enum.Enum):\n    IN_SCOPE = \"in_scope\"\n    OUT_OF_SCOPE = \"out_of_scope\"\n\n\nclass Program(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"programs\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    name = Column(String(255), nullable=False, unique=True)\n    created_at = Column(\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\n        default=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        nullable=False\n    )\n\n    # Relacionamentos\n    scopes = relationship(\"Scope\", back_populates=\"program\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\", lazy=\"selectin\")\n    assets = relationship(\"Asset\", back_populates=\"program\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\", lazy=\"selectin\")\n\n\nclass Scope(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"scopes\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    program_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"programs.id\", ondelete=\"CASCADE\"), nullable=False)\n    domain = Column(String(255), nullable=False)\n    scope_type = Column(SqlEnum(ScopeType), nullable=False, default=ScopeType.IN_SCOPE)\n\n    program = relationship(\"Program\", back_populates=\"scopes\")\n    assets = relationship(\"Asset\", back_populates=\"scope\", cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\")\n\n    __table_args__ = (\n        UniqueConstraint(\"program_id\", \"domain\", \"scope_type\", name=\"uq_program_domain_scope\"),\n    )\n\n\nclass Asset(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"assets\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\n    program_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"programs.id\", ondelete=\"CASCADE\"), nullable=False)\n    scope_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"scopes.id\", ondelete=\"SET NULL\"), nullable=True)\n    subdomain = Column(String(255), nullable=False)\n    resolved_ip = Column(String(64), nullable=True)\n    discovered_at = Column(\n        DateTime(timezone=True),\n        default=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        nullable=False\n    )\n\n    program = relationship(\"Program\", back_populates=\"assets\")\n    scope = relationship(\"Scope\", back_populates=\"assets\")\n\n    __table_args__ = (\n        UniqueConstraint(\"program_id\", \"subdomain\", name=\"uq_program_subdomain\"),\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.2. Validador de Escopo (`src/database/scope_validator.py`)\n\n```python\nimport fnmatch\nfrom typing import List\nfrom src.database.models import Scope, ScopeType\nfrom src.database.exceptions import OutOfScopeAssetException, NoMatchingInScopeException\n\n\nclass ScopeValidator:\n    \"\"\"Valida se um subdom\303\255nio descoberto \303\251 eleg\303\255vel com base nas regras do programa.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def domain_matches_pattern(subdomain: str, pattern: str) -> bool:\n        subdomain = subdomain.lower().strip()\n        pattern = pattern.lower().strip()\n\n        if pattern.startswith(\"*.\"):\n            base_domain = pattern[2:]\n            # Ex: *.uber.com d\303\241 match em api.uber.com e uber.com\n            return subdomain == base_domain or subdomain.endswith(\".\" + base_domain)\n        \n        return fnmatch.fnmatch(subdomain, pattern)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def validate_and_match_scope(cls, subdomain: str, scopes: List[Scope]) -> Scope:\n        # 1. Primeiro verifica se viola alguma regra de OUT-OF-SCOPE\n        for scope in scopes:\n            if scope.scope_type == ScopeType.OUT_OF_SCOPE:\n                if cls.domain_matches_pattern(subdomain, scope.domain):\n                    raise OutOfScopeAssetException(\n                        f\"Ativo \'{subdomain}\' pertence \303\240 regra Out-of-Scope: \'{scope.domain}\'\"\n                    )\n\n        # 2. Verifica se encaixa em alguma regra IN-SCOPE\n        matched_in_scope = None\n        for scope in scopes:\n            if scope.scope_type == ScopeType.IN_SCOPE:\n                if cls.domain_matches_pattern(subdomain, scope.domain):\n                    matched_in_scope = scope\n                    break\n\n        if not matched_in_scope:\n            raise NoMatchingInScopeException(\n                f\"Ativo \'{subdomain}\' n\303\243o pertence a nenhum escopo In-Scope cadastrado.\"\n            )\n\n        return matched_in_scope\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.3. Reposit\303\263rio Ass\303\255ncrono com Auto-Migra\303\247\303\243o (`src/database/repository.py`)\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.future import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n\nfrom src.database.models import Base, Program, Scope, ScopeType, Asset\nfrom src.database.scope_validator import ScopeValidator\n\n\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    \"\"\"Gerencia conex\303\243o SQLite e migra\303\247\303\265es autom\303\241ticas de inicializa\303\247\303\243o.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = \"recon.db\"):\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.engine = create_async_engine(f\"sqlite+aiosqlite:///{db_path}\", echo=False)\n        self.session_factory = sessionmaker(\n            self.engine, expire_on_commit=False, class_=AsyncSession\n        )\n\n    async def init_db(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifica se o banco existe e cria as tabelas automaticamente.\"\"\"\n        async with self.engine.begin() as conn:\n            await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    def get_session(self) -> AsyncSession:\n        return self.session_factory()\n\n\nclass ReconRepository:\n    def __init__(self, session: AsyncSession):\n        self.session = session\n\n    async def create_program(self, name: str) -> Program:\n        program = Program(name=name)\n        self.session.add(program)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(program)\n        return program\n\n    async def get_program_by_id(self, program_id: int) -> Optional[Program]:\n        result = await self.session.execute(\n            select(Program).where(Program.id == program_id)\n        )\n        return result.scalars().first()\n\n    async def add_scope(self, program_id: int, domain: str, scope_type: ScopeType) -> Scope:\n        scope = Scope(program_id=program_id, domain=domain, scope_type=scope_type)\n        self.session.add(scope)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(scope)\n        return scope\n\n    async def add_asset(self, program_id: int, subdomain: str, resolved_ip: Optional[str] = None) -> Asset:\n        program = await self.get_program_by_id(program_id)\n        if not program:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Programa ID {program_id} n\303\243o encontrado.\")\n\n        # Valida\303\247\303\243o contra In-Scope e Out-of-Scope antes da inser\303\247\303\243o\n        matched_scope = ScopeValidator.validate_and_match_scope(subdomain, program.scopes)\n\n        asset = Asset(\n            program_id=program_id,\n            scope_id=matched_scope.id,\n            subdomain=subdomain,\n            resolved_ip=resolved_ip\n        )\n        self.session.add(asset)\n        await self.session.commit()\n        await self.session.refresh(asset)\n        return asset\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. \360\237\216\257 Valida\303\247\303\243o da Fase 1\n\nTodos os 4 cen\303\241rios de teste exigidos por Delta foram cobertos:\n1. Inser\303\247\303\243o de `Program` e `Scope` (In/Out-of-Scope).\n2. Persist\303\252ncia e recarregamento relacional ass\303\255ncrono.\n3. Inser\303\247\303\243o bem-sucedida de subdom\303\255nios in-scope.\n4. **Bloqueio r\303\255gido de subdom\303\255nios pertencentes ao Out-of-Scope** (via exact match e wildcard matching).\n\n---\n\n> **L\303\255der de Opera\303\247\303\265es:** Voc\303\252 est\303\241 satisfeito com a arquitetura de persist\303\252ncia e a su\303\255te de testes da **FASE 1**, ou deseja algum ajuste no schema/regras antes de avan\303\247armos para a **FASE 2 (Motor de Execu\303\247\303\243o de Subprocessos / Terminal Resiliente)**?"
