  planner_response {
    response: "I have integrated **Google Drive** into **ReconCorrelator**:\n\n### Summary of Implementations\n\n- **OAuth 2.0 & Firebase Authentication**:\n  - Configured Google OAuth with Google Drive scopes for reading, writing, and organizing files.\n  - Implemented client-side authentication via Firebase Auth with official Google styling and secure in-memory token lifecycle management.\n\n- **Google Drive Cloud Vault & Hub (`Google Drive` Tab)**:\n  - **Dedicated Cloud Workspace**: Added a new tab in the top navigation bar to browse and manage cloud assets.\n  - **Auto-Organization**: Automatically creates and syncs files inside the designated `ReconCorrelator Reports` folder on your Google Drive.\n  - **1-Click Session Backup**: Instant upload of current attack surface snapshots in Markdown (`.md`) or raw JSON format.\n  - **Direct Import to Session**: Import previously saved scan results, subdomain lists, or findings directly from Google Drive back into the active workbench.\n  - **Custom Notes & PoCs**: Create Markdown research notes and proof-of-concept reports directly on Google Drive.\n  - **Destructive Operation Safety**: Implemented explicit confirmation modals before any file deletion on Google Drive.\n\n- **Enhanced Export Modal (`Salvar no Google Drive`)**:\n  - Integrated direct cloud export in the Export dialog, enabling single-click export of Bug Bounty reports (Markdown, JSON, or CSV) straight to Google Drive alongside standard local downloads."
    thinking: "**Summarizing The Implementation**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The build was successful. I\'m now crafting a concise and elegant summary of what we accomplished. The focus is on clarity and helpfulness, so I\'m outlining the key integrations. Specifically, I\'m detailing the Google OAuth and Firebase Authentication integration, noting how OAuth was configured with Google Drive scopes and the project client. Furthermore, I\'m highlighting the client-side token authentication using `GoogleAuthProvider` within Firebase Auth, emphasizing the in-memory token storage.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have integrated **Google Drive** into **ReconCorrelator**:\n\n### Summary of Implementations\n\n- **OAuth 2.0 & Firebase Authentication**:\n  - Configured Google OAuth with Google Drive scopes for reading, writing, and organizing files.\n  - Implemented client-side authentication via Firebase Auth with official Google styling and secure in-memory token lifecycle management.\n\n- **Google Drive Cloud Vault & Hub (`Google Drive` Tab)**:\n  - **Dedicated Cloud Workspace**: Added a new tab in the top navigation bar to browse and manage cloud assets.\n  - **Auto-Organization**: Automatically creates and syncs files inside the designated `ReconCorrelator Reports` folder on your Google Drive.\n  - **1-Click Session Backup**: Instant upload of current attack surface snapshots in Markdown (`.md`) or raw JSON format.\n  - **Direct Import to Session**: Import previously saved scan results, subdomain lists, or findings directly from Google Drive back into the active workbench.\n  - **Custom Notes & PoCs**: Create Markdown research notes and proof-of-concept reports directly on Google Drive.\n  - **Destructive Operation Safety**: Implemented explicit confirmation modals before any file deletion on Google Drive.\n\n- **Enhanced Export Modal (`Salvar no Google Drive`)**:\n  - Integrated direct cloud export in the Export dialog, enabling single-click export of Bug Bounty reports (Markdown, JSON, or CSV) straight to Google Drive alongside standard local downloads."
